---
// Intuition on the 12-week page: something you *experience*, not a subject
// we teach. Receiving information from the unconscious is half the practice
// (you can't acknowledge what you don't yet know), and across twelve weeks
// it simply happens more and more. Its deliberate training — receiving from
// someone else's voice — belongs to the certification course, linked at the
// foot. Copy drawn from the copy book, ch. 11 + 13 and quote bank A·5.
import { PRACTITIONER_URL } from './config';
---

<section class="tw-move tw-section" id="intuition">
  <div class="tw-move-inner">
    <div class="tw-move-media tw-move-media--square" data-reveal>
      <img
        class="tw-move-img"
        src="/media/library/svhgpt-04-sound-of-not-for.webp"
        alt="A seated figure sounding by candlelight, one hand at the heart, rings of warm light moving out through the room."
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </div>
    <div class="tw-move-text" data-reveal>
      <p class="tw-eyebrow">Intuition</p>
      <h2 class="tw-h2">A door to the unconscious — <em>that doesn’t need a couch.</em></h2>
      <p class="tw-p">
        A couple of minutes into sounding, the brain quiets. The busy daytime
        frequencies soften toward slower ones, and you become receptive to what
        usually stays below the surface. That’s when things start arriving that
        you didn’t think your way to: an age, an image, a name, a plain knowing
        about what this feeling is and where it began.
      </p>
      <p class="tw-p">
        That’s <strong>intuition</strong> — and it isn’t a gift a few people were
        handed at birth. It’s information coming up out of your own unconscious,
        through a channel finally wide enough to carry it. Your voice is the
        channel.
      </p>
      <p class="tw-move-quote">
        You’ll be surprised how much information you can get from your voice.
      </p>
      <p class="tw-p">
        This isn’t a mystical extra sitting on top of the practice. It’s half of
        it — nothing can be acknowledged while it’s still unknown, and the
        acknowledgment is where the healing happens. So you sound, and then you
        listen to what came back. Nobody grabs at it, either: trying hard is how
        the analytical mind gets back into the room. Receiving is the other
        orientation — gentle, open, allowing.
        <em>Passive in effort, active in attention.</em>
      </p>
      <p class="tw-p">
        Which is why it isn’t taught here as a subject of its own. Across twelve
        weeks you simply experience it more and more, until one day you catch
        what a sound is about before you’ve finished making it. Training it on
        purpose — receiving from <em>someone else’s</em> voice, learning where you
        end and they begin — is the work of the
        <a href={PRACTITIONER_URL}>certification course</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
